Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Of course!  Here's a simple example of an if/then statement in C:

```c
int dayOfWeek = Sunday;

if (dayOfWeek == Sunday) {
    // do something
}
else if (dayOfWeek == Monday) {
    // do another thing
}
else {
    // do something else
}
```

In this example, the if statement checks if the value of the variable `dayOfWeek` is equal to Sunday.  If the condition is true, the code inside the first block of the if statement will execute.  If the condition is false, the code inside the second block of the if statement will execute.  You can replace the code inside the if/then blocks with any other code you want to execute in each case.
